<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Orhan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1281–<a href="/years/1362">1362</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Orhan was the second ruler of the Ottoman state, succeeding his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/osman-i">Osman I</a>. He captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bursa">Bursa</a> in 1326 and made it the dynasty's first proper capital. His reign marked the transition of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> from a raiding frontier confederation into a territorial state.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/orhan.jpg" alt="Orhan" width="251" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Metehanzade_orhangazi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Osman’s victory over a Byzantine force at the Battle of Bapheus in 1302 established his military credibility, and his son <b>Orhan</b> captured Bursa in 1326, making it the dynasty’s first true capital and beginning the transition from raiding confederation to territorial state.</blockquote><a href="/empire/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire · Foundation</a></li><li><blockquote>An Ottoman army led by <b>Orhan</b> I defeated a Byzantine expeditionary force under Andronikos III at the Battle of Pelekanon.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/june-10">10 June in history</a></li><li><blockquote><b>Orhan</b> annexed the beylik, a process usually dated to around 1345, though resistance continued for some years.</blockquote><a href="/state/karasids">Karasids</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in Söğüt, in what is now <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>. Died in Bursa, in what is now <a href="/countries/turkey">Turkey</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=40.02,30.18&amp;year=1333" aria-label="Söğüt on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5293 732 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the birthplace of Orhan"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5743 1002h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5743 1002h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the birthplace. <a href="/atlas?at=40.02,30.18&amp;year=1333">What was here in 1333? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
